01:08:36,510 --> 01:08:38,560
As much as I love my mother.

1150
01:08:38,640 --> 01:08:43,200
It didn't affect me because I had a mind set.

1151
01:08:43,280 --> 01:08:46,440
My mind was set that this is a part of life.

1152
01:08:46,520 --> 01:08:52,880
I will be losing people. So when I had turned 40, I told my wife this categorically,

1153
01:08:52,960 --> 01:08:57,520
that the next five years of my life are the years of losses.

1154
01:08:57,600 --> 01:08:59,360
I'm going to lose a lot of people.

1155
01:08:59,440 --> 01:09:05,350
And this is a phase in a person's life that very rapidly you lose, because it's a generation.

1156
01:09:05,430 --> 01:09:09,190
There's a correlation, right? There's the same age in the front and back. Or some people get sick quickly.

1157
01:09:09,270 --> 01:09:14,310
Then they're going rapidly. I lost my uncle two years ago. Last year I lost my cousin.

1158
01:09:14,390 --> 01:09:17,305
He was like a brother to me.

1159
01:09:17,385 --> 01:09:17,693
Right?

1160
01:09:17,773 --> 01:09:18,860
In a one-year gap.

1161
01:09:18,940 --> 01:09:19,249
Right?

1162
01:09:19,329 --> 01:09:22,310
And those, I was very close with those people.

1163
01:09:22,390 --> 01:09:27,590
But like, that adaptability is there. That man, this is a part of life. It has to happen.

1164
01:09:27,670 --> 01:09:31,950
When I saw my uncle, I was like, he's not going to make it. When I saw my cousin.

1165
01:09:32,030 --> 01:09:38,950
When we found out that he was sick, he was not well, we came to see him, you know, the matter was a little further back.

1166
01:09:39,030 --> 01:09:45,950
When the C word was not revealed, I looked at my cousin and I was like, he's not with us this Eid.

1167
01:09:46,030 --> 01:09:51,950
I had thought about this Eid, he's not going to be with us. And within four months he passed away. Last stage cancer.

1168
01:09:52,030 --> 01:09:56,011
So this does not happen in everyone, right?

1169
01:09:56,091 --> 01:09:57,698
Some people grieve a lot.

1170
01:09:57,778 --> 01:09:59,650
And when my cousin passed away…

1171
01:09:59,730 --> 01:10:02,650
When my cousin passed away, I had told this story.

1172
01:10:02,730 --> 01:10:05,650
And he was lying dead.

1173
01:10:05,730 --> 01:10:08,650
And I was like, yeah, it had to happen.

1174
01:10:08,730 --> 01:10:11,650
It's good that he was not in so much pain. He was in a lot of pain.

1175
01:10:11,730 --> 01:10:16,650
But when I thought about my sister, who was very close to him because he was of the same age.

1176
01:10:16,730 --> 01:10:22,650
Then I cried because I was crying in relation to what he meant to my sister, what he meant to my brother.

1177
01:10:22,730 --> 01:10:25,730
So I had accepted that yes.

1178
01:10:26,220 --> 01:10:27,008
It had to happen.

1179
01:10:27,088 --> 01:10:30,537
But in relation to other people, I'm not sure if I'm making sense.

1180
01:10:30,617 --> 01:10:33,760
Please tell me if you also thought that way about something.

1181
01:10:33,840 --> 01:10:36,595
So yes, people's grieving period is different.

1182
01:10:36,675 --> 01:10:38,776
Some people can't get out of that grief.

1183
01:10:38,856 --> 01:10:41,299
That's why grieving therapies are also there.

1184
01:10:41,379 --> 01:10:41,679
Right?

1185
01:10:41,759 --> 01:10:45,137
Some people say that you shouldn't die with the dead.

1186
01:10:45,217 --> 01:10:47,404
But it's easier said than done.

1187
01:10:47,484 --> 01:10:50,187
Some people can't get out of it and should accept it.

1188
01:10:50,267 --> 01:10:52,620
So coming to your problem, sorry.

1189
01:10:54,320 --> 01:10:56,240
That's why I say, first get to know each other, get to know each other.

1190
01:10:56,320 --> 01:10:57,740
I am wearing three layers.

1191
01:10:57,820 --> 01:10:59,740
If you don't get along, then that's it.

1192
01:10:59,820 --> 01:11:03,240
Now, if you had this marathon running inside you,

1193
01:11:03,320 --> 01:11:07,740
somewhere or the other, you're clearly, if you're going to marathons, this and that,

1194
01:11:07,820 --> 01:11:11,740
then tell these things, that this is what I do, and then try to find out.

1195
01:11:11,820 --> 01:11:15,740
Now I got an email that my husband doesn't let me go to the gym alone.

1196
01:11:15,820 --> 01:11:17,740
He says, wear three layers.

1197
01:11:17,820 --> 01:11:20,820
I mean, like, I have to lose weight first.

1198
01:11:21,710 --> 01:11:25,630
and he says, if I'm traveling, you're not going to the gym.

1199
01:11:25,710 --> 01:11:28,630
So, please discuss these things first.

1200
01:11:28,710 --> 01:11:32,630
I want to do these things in the next 5 or 10 years.

1201
01:11:32,710 --> 01:11:35,630
These are my hobbies. These are the things that I like to do.

1202
01:11:35,710 --> 01:11:39,630
Or if it's about clothes, then discuss it first.

1203
01:11:39,710 --> 01:11:42,630
Some people are adamant that you have to do purdah.

1204
01:11:42,710 --> 01:11:44,630
Again, everyone has their own choices.

1205
01:11:44,710 --> 01:11:47,710
But if you don't want to do it, then these things should be communicated first.

1206
01:11:48,790 --> 01:11:52,070
It's not like you say yes right now, let me get married and then I'll explain.

1207
01:11:52,150 --> 01:11:55,290
Don't do that. That's cheating. Right?

1208
01:11:55,370 --> 01:12:02,530
That you temporarily listened to someone in a scheme, the other person believed you,

1209
01:12:02,610 --> 01:12:09,650
they joined you in a relationship, now you're saying that I'll use the stick.

1210
01:12:09,730 --> 01:12:11,930
That's not the nicest thing to do.

1211
01:12:12,010 --> 01:12:16,470
And then if you're doing it for a good cause, then that cheating is a good deed.

1212
01:12:16,550 --> 01:12:21,230
If the beginning of Islam is based on deceit, then that's not a good thing. Right?

1213
01:12:21,310 --> 01:12:28,470
So, anyway, I'm glad you opted out because clearly if you don't have the right mindset,

1214
01:12:28,550 --> 01:12:33,070
the right thoughts, then living life in such a place is a very long phase.

1215
01:12:33,150 --> 01:12:36,590
Although time passes very quickly, but it doesn't even pass.

1216
01:12:36,670 --> 01:12:40,350
If you are with a bad person, not a bad person, but a wrong person,

1217
01:12:40,430 --> 01:12:43,070
evil and good are subjective.

1218
01:12:43,150 --> 01:12:44,420
In my opinion, it is good and in my view…

1219
01:12:44,500 --> 01:12:45,840
He's doing the right thing in his eyes.

1220
01:12:45,920 --> 01:12:48,640
In someone else's eyes, maybe he's doing injustice.

1221
01:12:48,720 --> 01:12:50,020
Again, it's a subjective thing.

1222
01:12:50,100 --> 01:12:55,820
But a wrong person, a wrong person, who doesn't match with you, who doesn't join the Lego set,

1223
01:12:55,900 --> 01:12:57,420
then that becomes difficult.

1224
01:12:57,500 --> 01:12:58,820
Then that time doesn't pass.

1225
01:12:58,900 --> 01:13:00,520
And then you have to spend your whole life.

1226
01:13:00,600 --> 01:13:06,940
You are anyway a running woman, your life will be longer, because you are also exercising.

1227
01:13:07,020 --> 01:13:09,940
So why go through all that pain?

1228
01:13:10,020 --> 01:13:12,210
So please, ladies, apply.

1229
01:13:12,290 --> 01:13:15,010
to get rid of your parents,

1230
01:13:15,090 --> 01:13:17,610
don't go into another cage, that they are troubling you,

1231
01:13:17,690 --> 01:13:20,610
I don't want to get troubled by them, so I go here so they can trouble me.

1232
01:13:20,690 --> 01:13:22,810
What kind of living is this?

1233
01:13:22,890 --> 01:13:26,210
Jumping from one cage to another. Please,

1234
01:13:26,330 --> 01:13:29,310
do your due diligence, do your question and answer.

1235
01:13:29,390 --> 01:13:34,210
I'm saying this to men as well. Please, ask questions from every aspect.

1236
01:13:34,290 --> 01:13:36,210
What are the preferences in children?

1237
01:13:36,290 --> 01:13:40,290
How many children should be there? What's the recommended number you have in mind?

1238
01:13:40,640 --> 01:13:42,703
What is your point of view on daughters?

1239
01:13:42,783 --> 01:13:44,926
What are your aspirations for your sons?

1240
01:13:45,006 --> 01:13:46,713
How should children be raised?

1241
01:13:48,440 --> 01:13:55,440
This is an investment. When you go for a big investment, you discuss all the pros and cons.

1242
01:13:55,740 --> 01:14:00,154
And everyone thinks that if I am buying a house here or I am investing in this company,

1243
01:14:00,234 --> 01:14:01,799
then what are its pros and cons?

1244
01:14:01,879 --> 01:14:03,688
Will this product go into the market?

1245
01:14:03,768 --> 01:14:04,764
What will be its cost?

1246
01:14:04,844 --> 01:14:06,164
What will be its overheads?

1247
01:14:06,244 --> 01:14:06,544
Etc.

1248
01:14:06,624 --> 01:14:10,330
Similarly, this is like the biggest investment you are making in your life.

1249
01:14:10,410 --> 01:14:15,330
If you're not doing the due diligence, then if you don't do it today, you have to suffer tomorrow.

1250
01:14:15,410 --> 01:14:25,330
So it's better to know today and suffer a little and get on the side rather than you get into a situation and then that friction increases.

1251
01:14:25,410 --> 01:14:28,763
And where there is friction, things are not good.

1252
01:14:28,843 --> 01:14:30,030
Your day doesn't go well.

1253
01:14:30,110 --> 01:14:32,623
You wake up next to someone you don't even like.

1254
01:14:32,703 --> 01:14:33,650
That's not a way to live.

1255
01:14:33,730 --> 01:14:36,650
So please do your due diligence and I wish you well.

1256
01:14:36,730 --> 01:14:41,650
Take care and good luck to your trip in Karbala if you do it. Thank you.

1257
01:14:41,730 --> 01:14:47,730
Next question. I'm very hungry. Potatoes and Parathas are in the making. Yes.

1258
01:14:47,890 --> 01:14:49,651
We will burn the overseas people.

1259
01:14:49,731 --> 01:14:51,572
Why are Parathas not the same?

1260
01:14:51,652 --> 01:14:52,480
Outside Pakistan.

1261
01:14:52,560 --> 01:14:53,894
They're not the same man.

1262
01:14:53,974 --> 01:14:54,881
I don't know why.

1263
01:14:54,961 --> 01:14:55,682
What's missing?

1264
01:14:55,762 --> 01:14:56,569
Tell me.

1265
01:14:56,649 --> 01:14:58,650
Why is respect only for the successful?

1266
01:14:58,730 --> 01:15:00,890
Dear Junaid Bhaijaan, I hope you're doing well.

1267
01:15:00,970 --> 01:15:04,810
doing well, I wanted to share something that's been eating me up for a while.

1268
01:15:04,890 --> 01:15:09,810
And I feel like you're the one who can give it the Chittar Plus Wisdom treatment

1269
01:15:09,890 --> 01:15:14,170
it deserves. I'm 27 living in a typical Indian joint family where respect is directly

1270
01:15:14,250 --> 01:15:17,890
proportional to your salary slip. No matter how much I help at home, how respectfully

1271
01:15:17,970 --> 01:15:22,295
I talk or how responsible I am, it all means nothing because according to the elders,

1272
01:15:22,375 --> 01:15:23,873
beta abhi settle nahi hua hai.

1273
01:15:23,953 --> 01:15:26,330
Meanwhile, my cousin who just got a fancy job.

1274
01:15:26,940 --> 01:15:30,327
In Dubai is treated like he's the second coming of Shah Jahan.

1275
01:15:30,407 --> 01:15:39,803
The funny thing we have the same level of education but since he earns in Dirhams and I earn in Indian Rupees his words are gospel and mine are background noise.

1276
01:15:39,883 --> 01:15:42,913
I work over 10 hours a day sometimes even on weekends.

1277
01:15:42,993 --> 01:15:47,797
On top of that I take complete care of my parents, their health, their doctor visits,

1278
01:15:47,877 --> 01:15:48,726
their well being.

1279
01:15:48,806 --> 01:15:52,710
I also do household chores on Sundays making sure things are in place.

1280
01:15:52,820 --> 01:15:57,060
But when it comes to respect, there is no respect like a cover.

1281
01:15:57,140 --> 01:16:03,860
If he suggests something, even if it's common sense, the elder is not like he's giving out free TED talks.

1282
01:16:03,940 --> 01:16:08,060
But if I say the same thing, when you settle, then talk about this.

1283
01:16:08,300 --> 01:16:12,245
Meaning the person is working hard day and night, looking after the housework,

1284
01:16:12,325 --> 01:16:16,511
taking care of the parents, but because the salary is not in foreign currency,

1285
01:16:16,591 --> 01:16:18,260
then respect is also in discount.

1286
01:16:18,700 --> 01:16:20,253
Is this how Desi families work?

1287
01:16:20,333 --> 01:16:20,633
Yes.

1288
01:16:20,713 --> 01:16:24,574
Is there any way to gain respect without having to turn into a walking ATM?

1289
01:16:24,654 --> 01:16:24,954
No.

1290
01:16:25,034 --> 01:16:28,380
Or should I just shut up and hustle till the day magically?

1291
01:16:28,460 --> 01:16:31,278
They magically decide I'm worthy.

1292
01:16:31,358 --> 01:16:33,307
Would love to hear your take on this.

1293
01:16:33,387 --> 01:16:35,100
Respectfully, a Desi struggler.

1294
01:16:46,350 --> 01:16:48,270
We take care of our parents and everything.

1295
01:16:48,350 --> 01:16:55,270
And this is the same thing in this, our older generation has the same scene.

1296
01:16:55,350 --> 01:16:58,270
That you have to respect by giving your pocket.

1297
01:16:58,350 --> 01:17:00,849
You will remember that in the last email,

1298
01:17:00,929 --> 01:17:06,727
there was an email in the last episode that the aunt asks immediately on the flight,

1299
01:17:06,807 --> 01:17:08,270
what is the visa status?

1300
01:17:08,350 --> 01:17:14,350
Because they are computing that you have to respect or get respect.

1301
01:17:14,580 --> 01:17:19,660
So financial status, visa status and all these things are why they gauge.

1302
01:17:19,740 --> 01:17:24,060
Whenever they meet, they instantly ask, which car is this? Which school are the kids going to?

1303
01:17:24,140 --> 01:17:26,980
It's because they're gauging.

1304
01:17:27,060 --> 01:17:31,500
Because in our society, respect is not inherently inherent to a person.

1305
01:17:31,580 --> 01:17:33,620
And it's not inherent to the value system either.

1306
01:17:33,700 --> 01:17:36,540
It's about what that person can offer.

1307
01:17:36,620 --> 01:17:38,540
Or what that person can give.

1308
01:17:38,620 --> 01:17:40,620
So when you live in, when you're a product of such.

1309
01:17:40,730 --> 01:17:42,132
Such a society is there.

1310
01:17:42,212 --> 01:17:44,373
I have gone through the same thing.

1311
01:17:44,453 --> 01:17:48,642
I remember my brother, my eldest brother, when he was working,

1312
01:17:48,722 --> 01:17:51,683
he was practically running the household.

1313
01:17:51,763 --> 01:17:53,350
So he had a lot of respect.

1314
01:17:53,430 --> 01:17:58,768
And we would wait for him to come home and then we'll eat together.

1315
01:17:58,848 --> 01:18:02,393
He will get the preferential food and everything.

1316
01:18:02,473 --> 01:18:06,000
And we would be told to not, not to disturb, not to show off.

1317
01:18:06,080 --> 01:18:08,200
don't steal, you know, I came for work.

1318
01:18:08,280 --> 01:18:13,700
But like he had his own challenges after a point.

1319
01:18:13,780 --> 01:18:15,100
He got bored.

1320
01:18:15,180 --> 01:18:16,400
The same job satisfaction.

1321
01:18:16,480 --> 01:18:17,400
He just left the job.

1322
01:18:17,480 --> 01:18:22,700
And then I saw that respect was empty within two weeks.

1323
01:18:22,780 --> 01:18:27,200
And then the same taunts that others used to hear, those taunts have also shifted there.

1324
01:18:27,280 --> 01:18:32,280
So yes, you are respected only on the basis of what you can offer.

1325
01:18:32,920 --> 01:18:34,840
Sadly, that is the thing.

1326
01:18:34,920 --> 01:18:40,240
Now, what you can do is don't seek validation.

1327
01:18:40,320 --> 01:18:42,240
Just do the right thing.

1328
01:18:42,320 --> 01:18:46,240
And of course, as long as you're doing the right thing,

1329
01:18:46,320 --> 01:18:48,240
I'm coming, mom.

1330
01:18:48,320 --> 01:18:50,240
I'm coming. Thank you.

1331
01:18:50,320 --> 01:18:54,240
So, just because you're doing, what was I saying?

1332
01:18:54,320 --> 01:18:56,240
You have to keep doing the right thing.

1333
01:18:56,320 --> 01:18:58,740
That's what I believe. A person has to keep himself right.

1334
01:18:58,820 --> 01:19:00,820
Things eventually fall in place.

1335
01:19:01,040 --> 01:19:05,160
Even if you don't, if people are worthy, they will give you worth.

1336
01:19:05,240 --> 01:19:09,800
Even if they are not, God is watching. Karma is there. Right?

1337
01:19:09,880 --> 01:19:13,560
So you keep doing the right thing and everything will fall in its place.

1338
01:19:13,640 --> 01:19:17,560
As far as the outside world is concerned, they have more respect.

1339
01:19:17,640 --> 01:19:22,816
In our country, we have always put the invaders first.

1340
01:19:22,896 --> 01:19:25,480
It's like a very desi thing.

1341
01:19:27,410 --> 01:19:29,649
is a little superior, it is heard more.

1342
01:19:29,729 --> 01:19:33,974
Like for example, I know a household where the son is equally smart,

1343
01:19:34,054 --> 01:19:37,730
but the brother-in-law is more active in that house.

1344
01:19:37,810 --> 01:19:38,110
Why?

1345
01:19:38,190 --> 01:19:42,783
Because they look up that yes, it's the daughter's house, this and that.

1346
01:19:42,863 --> 01:19:46,530
Although, you know, the son is equally smart or even better.

1347
01:19:46,610 --> 01:19:47,996
It's like the same thing.

1348
01:19:48,076 --> 01:19:50,927
So the day you go out, you will also be respected.

1349
01:19:51,007 --> 01:19:54,160
The day you start earning more, you will be respected.

1350
01:19:54,340 --> 01:20:00,660
So this is it. Preferential treatment is necessary. They lie when they say that all the kids are the same.

1351
01:20:00,740 --> 01:20:04,860
And the one who is more like us feels bad. The same chicken curry at home.

1352
01:20:04,940 --> 01:20:11,260
So I would suggest you to keep doing what you're doing. Work hard. Upskill yourself.

1353
01:20:11,340 --> 01:20:17,260
And you know, with time you will essentially start earning more and more.

1354
01:20:17,340 --> 01:20:21,960
And serve. Maybe one day they'll see it. And don't do it because-

1355
01:20:22,040 --> 01:20:25,720
Do it because you want them to see it. Do it because you like doing it.

1356
01:20:25,800 --> 01:20:30,960
Like if you want to serve your parents, don't do it because they'll acknowledge you as a good son.

1357
01:20:31,040 --> 01:20:34,320
Do it because that's your inherent purpose to do.

1358
01:20:34,400 --> 01:20:39,320
You have to take care of your parents. Whether they pay attention or not, that's their business.

1359
01:20:39,400 --> 01:20:43,600
If they're grateful, they will see it. If they're ungrateful, they won't see it.

1360
01:20:43,680 --> 01:20:47,320
That's their problem. You do your part. Okay?

1361
01:20:47,890 --> 01:20:54,290
I tell everyone to do their part with a pure heart and not think that I will get a reward for it.

1362
01:20:54,370 --> 01:20:58,290
I will still get a reward but not think that I am doing it because there is a reward.

1363
01:20:58,370 --> 01:21:00,610
You do it because you love your parents, right?

1364
01:21:00,690 --> 01:21:07,602
So if they feel God's mercy, then mercy will break the door of their heart,

1365
01:21:07,682 --> 01:21:11,970
closed heart and then they will essentially start to respect you.

1366
01:21:12,770 --> 01:21:18,690
Why do you need it? What Padma Shri award do you want with respect?

1367
01:21:18,770 --> 01:21:24,690
Do your thing. If it makes you feel useful, happy and content.

1368
01:21:24,770 --> 01:21:29,690
Who is this rude person? Does anyone ring the bell at 9 AM at someone's house?

1369
01:21:29,770 --> 01:21:34,690
So if you feel content, that should be your goal.

1370
01:21:34,770 --> 01:21:37,670
That I like doing house chores.

1371
01:21:38,060 --> 01:21:43,570
It's my nieces. I like doing house chores. I like to help out.

1372
01:21:45,600 --> 01:21:51,040
if I make their lives easier in one way or the other, it generally makes me happy.

1373
01:21:51,120 --> 01:21:56,440
That should be your goal. Not that I should get respect. Why do you need respect?

